# CropperBackgroundWrapper

`CropperBackgroundWrapper` is the default `backgroundWrapperComponent` of the croppers. It wraps the background image and the stencil in a [`TransformableImage`](/docs/components/TransformableImage), which turns mouse drags, the wheel and touch gestures into image transforms, and forwards those to the cropper.

```
StretchableBoundary
└─ CropperBackgroundWrapper → TransformableImage
   ├─ CropperBackgroundImage
   └─ stencil
```

Gestures on the stencil itself don't reach it: the stencil's draggable parts stop those events, so dragging the stencil never pans the image.

## Usage

The cropper renders it for you. Configure it through the cropper's `backgroundWrapperProps`:

```svelte
<!-- Allow two-finger rotation, and turn off zooming with the wheel -->
<Cropper
	{src}
	backgroundWrapperProps={{
		rotateImage: true,
		scaleImage: { touch: true, wheel: false }
	}}
/>
```

```svelte
<!-- Make the image impossible to move or zoom -->
<Cropper {src} backgroundWrapperProps={{ moveImage: false, scaleImage: false }} />
```

## Props

| Prop          | Type                                                           | Default     | Description                                                                                                                                  |
| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `cropper`     | `{ transformImage, transformImageEnd, getTransitions }`        | —           | **Required.** Passed by the cropper.                                                                                                         |
| `moveImage`   | `boolean` \| `{ touch?: boolean; mouse?: boolean }`            | `true`      | Moving the image by dragging it. `true` turns on both touch and mouse.                                                                       |
| `scaleImage`  | `boolean` \| `ScaleImageOptions`                                | `true`      | Zooming the image with a pinch (`touch`) or the wheel (`wheel`). `true` means `{ touch: true, wheel: { ratio: 0.1 } }`.                     |
| `rotateImage` | `boolean` \| `{ touch?: boolean }`                              | `false`     | Rotating the image with a two-finger gesture.                                                                                                |
| `timeout`     | `number`                                                       | `500`       | How long after the last wheel event, in milliseconds, the wheel gesture counts as finished. Read once, when the component mounts.             |
| `disabled`    | `boolean`                                                      | —           | Ignores every gesture and lets the browser handle the events (so the page can scroll). Passed by the cropper.                                 |
| `class`       | `ClassValue`                                                   | —           | Classes for the root element. The cropper passes `advanced-cropper__background-wrapper` plus `backgroundWrapperClassName`.                 |
| `style`       | `string`                                                       | —           | Inline style for the root element.                                                                                                           |
| `children`    | `Snippet`                                                      | —           | The background and the stencil.                                                                                                              |

```ts
interface ScaleImageOptions {
	touch?: boolean;
	// The ratio is the zoom step of one wheel notch.
	wheel?: boolean | { ratio?: number };
	adjustStencil?: boolean;
}
```

`adjustStencil` is part of the type for compatibility but is not read here. Use the cropper's `transformImage` setting instead.

While a transition runs, gestures are ignored, so they can't fight the animation.

The option objects are normalized by the exported [`useMoveImageOptions`](/docs/hooks/useMoveImageOptions), [`useScaleImageOptions`](/docs/hooks/useScaleImageOptions) and [`useRotateImageOptions`](/docs/hooks/useRotateImageOptions), which you can reuse in a custom wrapper.

## Custom background wrappers

Pass your own component as `backgroundWrapperComponent` to change how gestures behave, for example to require a modifier key for the wheel. It receives `cropper`, `class`, `disabled`, a `children` snippet and everything in `backgroundWrapperProps`. It must render `children` and apply `class` to its root element. Building it on [`TransformableImage`](/docs/components/TransformableImage) with an `onEvent` handler is the simplest route.

## CSS classes

The component adds no classes of its own. Its root element carries the `class` it receives, which with the default cropper is `advanced-cropper__background-wrapper` (absolutely positioned to fill the boundary).
